Derived components
------------------

The following parts are based on GravesX implementations and keep their
attribution headers in the source files:

* dev.qsdeath.util.ExperienceUtil
  Based on com.ranull.graves.util.ExperienceUtil (total experience calculation).

* dev.qsdeath.util.ItemCodec
  Based on the Bukkit object-stream inventory serialisation used by
  com.ranull.graves.util.Base64Util and com.ranull.graves.util.InventoryUtil.

* dev.qsdeath.display.HeadService
  Based on the skull profile/texture handling of GravesX
  (SkinTextureUtil and SkinTextureUtil_post_1_21_9).

* dev.qsdeath.display.NameplateService
  TextDisplay nameplate technique derived from
  dev.cwhead.GravesX.manager.TextDisplayManager.

* Architectural concepts (death capture before item removal, text-display
  holograms, evidence records, item safety on restart) follow the GravesX
  architecture as described in docs/AUDIT-AND-DESIGN.md.

Deliberately not reused
-----------------------

GravesX is a 67k-line general-purpose grave plugin with runtime library
downloading (Libby), H2/MySQL/PostgreSQL/MariaDB support, 40+ soft integrations,
compass teleportation, grave GUIs and many features that conflict with the qS
Death System specification (single SQLite database, police-only evidence access,
no public teleportation, no resource packs). Those components were replaced by
a focused implementation; the audit report documents the decision and the
compatibility findings.

